{"module":"Term 2","title":"Unit 8 — Science and Technology","description":"Inventions and gadgets, the future (will / going to), first conditional, predictions.","intro":"This unit is about inventions, technology in daily life and the future.","objectifs":["Talk about inventions and devices.","Use will and be going to.","Make predictions and use the first conditional."],"cours":[{"t":"Vocabulary","h":"<ul><li>an invention, an inventor, a device, a gadget, a smartphone, artificial intelligence, a robot</li><li>to invent, to discover, to download, to charge, to browse</li></ul>"},{"t":"Grammar: the future","h":"<ul><li><b>will</b> + base verb: predictions and quick decisions — <i>Robots <b>will</b> do many jobs.</i></li><li><b>be going to</b> + base verb: plans and evidence — <i>I’m <b>going to</b> study computer science. Look at the clouds: it’s going to rain.</i></li></ul><div class=\"formula key\">First conditional: If + present simple, … will + base verb</div><div class=\"box ex\"><span class=\"box-title\">Example</span><p>If you <b>charge</b> your phone, it <b>will work</b> all day.</p></div>"},{"t":"Communication: predicting","h":"<ul><li>I think / I’m sure … will…</li><li>Perhaps / maybe … will…</li><li>I don’t think … will…</li></ul>"}],"recap":"will = prediction / instant decision ; going to = plan / evidence. First conditional: If + present, will + verb (never “will” after “if”). invent = create something new ; discover = find something that existed.","cards":[["will","Prediction, quick decision"],["going to","Plan, evidence"],["If + present","… will + verb"],["invent / discover","create new / find existing"]],"exercises":{"facile":[{"type":"qcm","q":"If it rains, we ___ at home.","choices":["will stay","stay","stayed","would stay"],"answer":0,"explain":"First conditional: if + present, will + base verb."},{"type":"direct","q":"A person who invents things is an ___.","accept":["inventor"],"display":"inventor","explain":"invent → inventor."},{"type":"qcm","q":"I think robots ___ teach in schools one day.","choices":["will","are","did","have"],"answer":0,"explain":"Prediction → will."}],"moyen":[{"type":"qcm","q":"I’ve decided: I ___ become an engineer.","choices":["am going to","will be","went to","have"],"answer":0,"explain":"A plan / decision made before → going to."},{"type":"direct","q":"Complete: “If you ___ (press) this button, the machine will start.”","accept":["press"],"display":"press","explain":"After “if”: present simple, not will."},{"type":"qcm","q":"Fleming ___ penicillin in 1928.","choices":["discovered","invented","downloaded","charged"],"answer":0,"explain":"Penicillin existed in nature: it was discovered."}],"difficile":[{"type":"qcm","q":"Find the correct sentence:","choices":["If we use technology wisely, it will help us.","If we will use technology wisely, it helps us.","If we will use technology wisely, it will help us.","If we used technology wisely, it will help us."],"answer":0,"explain":"Never “will” in the if-clause of the first conditional."},{"type":"direct","q":"Complete: “Look at those black clouds! It ___ rain.” (3 words)","accept":["is going to","'s going to"],"display":"is going to","explain":"Evidence now → be going to."},{"type":"qcm","q":"“I’m thirsty.” — “OK, I ___ get you some water.”","choices":["’ll","’m going to","get","got"],"answer":0,"explain":"Instant decision → will (’ll)."}]}}